WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:11.501
Any decomposition of a function backpropagates correctly if each local derivative is right; frameworks fuse operations for speed and stability, not correctness.

3
00:00:11.781 --> 00:00:23.344
A neuron is tanh of an affine map, a layer is many neurons, an MLP is layers in sequence; a layer with n inputs and m outputs has m(n + 1) parameters.

4
00:00:23.624 --> 00:00:28.872
A loss reduces “how wrong” to one number; squared error’s gradient is twice the error.

5
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:36.917
Gradient descent steps against the gradient; the Taylor expansion says small steps help, and the learning rate decides how small.

6
00:00:37.197 --> 00:00:39.885
Zero the gradients before every backward pass.

7
00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:44.197
Next week: the same machinery, applied to predicting the next character.
